Redis 7.2.16 blocking-list tests: close both auxiliary clients on every exit.
The two WATCH fixtures can fail before their explicit closes when a server
refuses WATCH. Keep their commands, expected results and original errors;
close every successfully created client and wait for the blocked-client count
to return to its entry value before propagating the outcome. Cleanup failures
are reported separately when an earlier error already owns the outcome.
Apply to Firn, Redis reference and external targets alike. Retire when the
pinned upstream fixtures provide equivalent exception-safe cleanup.

Source:
https://github.com/redis/redis/blob/7.2.16/tests/unit/type/list.tcl

